    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: ab4a9593826fa623c0d58ac4b527ebc30601f294 -->\n**Review (M3, safety tier): needs changes before merge.** The drill and bore fix is sound and well pinned, but the thread-mill pin fails at this head.\n\n**What looks good**\n- `loop_tol`/`is_rim` read a loop at the plain tolerance only when every vertex lies within 2 µm of a declared circle; otherwise the loop stays tightened, and that is pinned.\n- Both the law-point and the Boundary wall readings use it. The solid law stays tightened.\n- Mutation checks were each caught by `model_excess` and/or `coarse_rims`: always-tight, wall-only, law-point-only, `is_rim` always true, `RIM_MATCH` 0.5, Drill or Bore dropped from `rims_of`, and no rims filled.\n\n**Local results** (merged with main)\n- camcraft-sim: all pass.\n- app: `coarse_contain`, `coarse_laws`, `verify`, `mill2d_c`, `thread_mill_rim`, `bore_entry`, `bore_facet_sagitta`, `blind_floor`, `drill_reach`, `hole_wall_flats`, `hole_wall_pins`, `model_fidelity` and `solid_law_goldens` pass.\n- Clippy is clean.\n- **`coarse_rims`: 4 pass, 1 FAIL**, on the PR head alone too:\n```\na_thread_mill_reads_the_same_near_the_bound_as_at_full_fidelity\ncrates/app/tests/coarse_rims.rs:205: left: [Gouge{at:20}..Gouge{at:39}]  right: []\n```\n\n**Requested before merge**\n1. **The Thread arm of `rims_of` is dead.** `material_source.rs` declares `(xy, radius)` for the Thread arm, but main's #1071 (`generate.rs` ~2140, `thread_rims::major_rims`) gives the thread region a disk at `r + depth`. So the declared circle traces no loop, and a thread mill on a coarse model is still read tightened. That is the conservative direction, but it contradicts the PR body, the decision file and the pin. Fix it one of two ways:\n   - declare the major circle (`r + THREAD_DEPTH_PER_PITCH * pitch`); or\n   - drop Thread from `rims_of`, drop the thread test, and correct the body and the decision file.\n\n**Notes**\n- Merge-time refresh: `generate.rs` only. Take main's `let ctx = VerifyContext{..}` and add `rims: &rims` after `model_excess: material.excess`.\n- The `DepthLaw::Contain` guard around `rims` has no pin. Low risk.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
